# KNOWN GAP (todo/t0681) -- dereferencing a `Box[Callable[...]]` is rejected
# with a diagnostic that denies its own premise:
#
#     error[E_DerefNonBox]: cannot dereference `*` a value of type
#     `Box[Callable[int(int)]]` -- `*` requires a `Box[T]`
#
# The value IS a `Box[T]`. Both construction spellings (`Box.new(...)` and
# `Box[Callable[int(int)]](...)`) hit it identically, so it is independent of
# the constructor-vs-method split that R49 Track A1-IDENTITY closed.
#
# DECIDE -- the message is wrong under both readings:
#   (a) the shape is meaningful, `*f` yields the boxed Callable, and this
#       program prints 42; or
#   (b) a `Box[Callable[...]]` genuinely may not be dereferenced -- then the
#       diagnostic must say WHY, because "requires a `Box[T]`" is not a reason
#       a reader can act on when the value is one.
#
# DISCRIMINATED FROM `box_callable_call_through_box_undefined_function.gg`:
# there the boxed payload is a `Callable`-typed STRUCT FIELD, there is no
# closure environment behind it, and it ICEs at GIR VALIDATION. This one is
# rejected cleanly at CHECK time. Different phase, different mechanism.
#
# INTENDED (asserted below): prints 42.
# RED-verified 2026-09-04: rejected at check time with the message above.

void main():
    Box[Callable[int(int)]] f = Box.new((int n): n * 2)
    print((*f)(21))
